e rules.\n","tags":["A-CheckStyle"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":5,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":12,"deletions":16}}},{"hash":"29fd5e8e7538cd881908775f2ee269be9647052e","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add NotMarth JavaFX interface","messageBody":"Add a cross-platform JavaFX launcher and command window that reuse the\nexisting parser, commands, storage, and tactical response messages. Keep\nthe console entry point available for automated testing and CLI use.\n","tags":["Level-10"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":15,"deletions":1},"java":{"insertions":122,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"b5cee1e9e6ac0ff4b50a0211e2d2b265dd47a433","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add varargs task list constructor","messageBody":"Provide a concise constructor for callers that already have an initial\nsequence of tasks while retaining the list-based constructor used by\nstorage loading.\n","tags":["A-Varargs"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":23,"deletions":0}}}]},{"date":"2026-09-02T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"c180921fffa6c475dca3f467d5d546b7a5861569","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Match JavaFX tutorial GUI style","messageBody":"Organize the Level-10 interface around FXML views, reusable dialog boxes,\nand CSS styling consistent with the JavaFX tutorial repository. Keep the\nNotMarth command backend and console behavior unchanged.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":94,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":165,"deletions":65}}},{"hash":"40febc9041a4636207047ea2db269ffdf44e8274","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Restore original chat behavior","messageBody":"Preserve the original Level-10 welcome text and close the JavaFX window\nwhen the bye command is entered. Keep the FXML, CSS, and dialog layout\nchanges independent from command behavior.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":17,"deletions":8}}},{"hash":"b53937f1ed791a806b401b551a437d2e4f22b6e1","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix dialog box stylesheet loading","messageBody":"Load the dialog stylesheet explicitly after FXML construction so user and\nNotMarth messages render with the intended speech-bubble styling. Keep\ncommand processing and the tutorial repository unchanged.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":2,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"0c4465dfb455d0b9c834f69bc5de9d4a21c0068b","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027branch-level-10\u0027","messageBody":"","tags":["v0.2"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-09-08T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"1a8309b99bc2505708d0a2cbf5244cf2965bc276","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add assertions for task list invariants","messageBody":"TaskList relies on its capacity and task-number checks to preserve\nits internal state.\n\nAdd assertions for the validated capacity and task-number invariants so\nunexpected violations are detected during development without changing\nnormal command behavior.\n","tags":["A-FullCommitMessage"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":2,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"5da7deaf9a8a118da96adab31ee739b8824cd852","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Centralize parser command guidance","messageBody":"Parser repeats the list of supported commands in multiple error\nmessages, which makes future command updates easy to miss.\n\nStore the shared command guidance in one constant and reuse it in both\nmessages so the wording stays consistent as the command set evolves.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":4,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"ef72f518df71b766a26c41f09860b7f551067a19","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Use streams for indexed task filtering","messageBody":"The find and on commands both scan task indexes with explicit loops\nand duplicate match-state handling.\n\nUse streams to collect matching indexes before displaying results. This\nkeeps original task numbers and ordering while making the filtering logic\nmore declarative and sharing the same empty-result flow.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":26,"deletions":27}}},{"hash":"f9d91b41fa56b46832a6ef307cd73bbc39fc416e","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Document assumptions with Java assertions","messageBody":"The task model, parser, task list, and storage layer rely on several\ninvariants that are not visible at the point where they are consumed.\n\nDocument these assumptions with assertion messages and focused comments:\nnon-null model inputs, valid task-list capacity and numbering, append\npostconditions, parser inputs, and safe storage subtype casts.\n\nKeep user-facing validation unchanged so assertions remain development-time\nchecks rather than a replacement for normal error handling.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":21,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"7ad70923bc86b1389688d91ebdb227bd8739cfcc","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #1 from ooixs/branch-A-Assertions","messageBody":"TaskList relies on its capacity and task-number checks to preserve\nits internal state.\n\nAdd assertions for the validated capacity and task-number invariants so\nunexpected violations are detected during development without changing\nnormal command behavior.","tags":["A-Assertions"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"40dbfbeeb3f19aa2e447d7bc1ce8f9df09ce9856","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into branch-A-CodeQuality","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"eb46c95795d726985a74fec7bce4f4dd07e4bf4e","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into branch-A-Streams","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"82d2445cb70542ab8265a08f8b9565844c924d88","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Simplify task command parsing","messageBody":"Parser.createTask combines the parsing rules for three task types in\none deeply nested method, making the common dispatch logic harder to read.\n\nSplit ToDo, Deadline, and Event parsing into focused helpers and use guard\nclauses for malformed arguments. Keep each helper at one level of\nabstraction so the valid parsing path is easier to follow without changing\nany accepted commands or error messages.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":69,"deletions":45}}},{"hash":"3c9b7c96add4dc56055483073f3b312d91012e86","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Simplify archive record parsing","messageBody":"Storage.parseTask and splitRecord mix validation, conversion, and escape\nhandling in dense methods that are difficult to scan and maintain.\n\nExtract task construction and escaped-character handling into focused\nhelpers. Keep validation and persistence behavior unchanged while making\nthe normal archive-loading path easier to follow.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":30,"deletions":21}}},{"hash":"138163397d6ffba32812900ff9f5ec1ba70ca9eb","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #2 from ooixs/branch-A-CodeQuality","messageBody":"Branch a code quality","tags":["A-CodeQuality"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"92aa927202c25cf77c84223b2d65a2e1b9623abf","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Use streams for formatter matching","messageBody":"DateTimeParser scans ordered formatter lists and returns the first\nformat that accepts the input.\n\nUse stream pipelines with Optional results and findFirst to express this\nsearch directly. Keep date-time formats ahead of date-only formats while\nisolating exception handling in small helpers, so the parsing priority and\nfailure behavior remain explicit.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":29,"deletions":14}}},{"hash":"845dc4bb1fc7a34946aeb0eca998d53d19e95245","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into branch-A-Streams","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"5f0423fafffb88df110933b1dc948a142fca8330","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #3 from ooixs/branch-A-Streams","messageBody":"Branch a streams","tags":["A-Streams"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"2aff833139ca028d27bc6fa484a55720ecca1f44","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add contact management extension","messageBody":"Introduce standalone contact records with commands to add, list, find,\nand delete contacts.\n\nPersist contacts alongside existing tasks while retaining the original task\ncommands and archive records for backward compatibility. Document and cover\nthe new workflow with unit and UI tests for the tuitionbook use case.\n","tags":["BCD-Extension"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":417,"deletions":27},"md":{"insertions":84,"deletions":11}}}]},{"date":"2026-09-09T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"71045e836b59e9d312f2e1032baffe2170eb1a2c","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"update test naming conventions","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":24,"deletions":24},"md":{"insertions":7,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"c091b98c9f3d45674dbe6a9b6895fb2238c7d80b","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"add other code quality changes","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":273,"deletions":263},"md":{"insertions":5,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"68a40bf9f080ae5540d11101ea6ef8eab2315a2c","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"add better GUI","messageBody":"","tags":["A-BetterGui"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":39,"deletions":48},"java":{"insertions":29,"deletions":11}}},{"hash":"5ae6bd973b4f9b25785f7c89b31634d2c93b5abc","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"improve personality","messageBody":"","tags":["A-Personality"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":2,"deletions":1},"java":{"insertions":3,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"05fca8eb6d561b86a96cc23f6a739a247b185061","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"add more error handling","messageBody":"","tags":["A-MoreErrorHandling"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":208,"de